1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,200
东北老话：姑爷进门，小鸡断魂
Dongbei saying: son-in-law comes, the chicken's doomed

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:04,400
新姑爷回门，老丈人必做这道菜
A new son-in-law's visit means one must-cook dish

3
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:06,600
这是招待贵客的最高规格
The highest honor you can serve a guest

4
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:08,800
一只养半年、满地跑的笨鸡
A free-range hen raised half a year

5
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,000
配东北山里的野生榛蘑
Paired with wild hazel mushrooms from the hills

6
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,200
小火咕嘟一个多小时
Simmered low for over an hour

7
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:15,400
榛蘑吸饱鸡汤，比肉还香
The mushrooms drink the broth — better than the meat

8
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:17,600
伐木工人野鸡炖榛蘑，就是它的雏形
Loggers' wild-fowl stew was its earliest form

9
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:19,800
也是年三十桌上的压轴主菜
Also the centerpiece of New Year's Eve

10
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:22,000
锅包肉、铁锅炖、炖粉条…压轴是它
Guobaorou, iron-pot, glass noodles… this crowns them

11
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:24,200
一句老话，就是东北的待客之道
One old saying is Dongbei's way of welcome

12
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:26,200
你心里的东北硬菜天花板，是哪道？
Your ultimate Dongbei dish — which one is it?

13
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:28,300
「东北硬菜」四道更新完毕，评论区见
Four Dongbei classics, complete — see you below
